+# Windhawk V1 beta 1 execution plan
+
+Continue the accepted V1 phases under D-0007 and the operator's beta request.
+This is refinement of the existing candidate, not a new repository or feature
+reduction. Sole repository writer; read-only delegated review is allowed.
+
+1. **Phase 2 foundation:** review controller/presentation boundaries, fix
+   observed lifecycle defects, preserve final joins and independent emergency
+   cleanup. Add version-consistent build provenance and fail-closed receipts.
+2. **Phase 3 parity:** retain P01–P11, exercise saved settings and state changes
+   through real production adapters on hidden test windows, improve diagnostics
+   and input behavior where review finds concrete defects.
+3. **Phase 4 savers:** test independent concurrent owned sessions via the real
+   controller/reconciler, strengthen child-window health after startup, retain
+   black fallback and no automatic relaunch loop. Simulated displays stay
+   explicitly distinct from physical monitor evidence.
+4. **Phase 5 verification:** pure policy/configuration; storage/process/media
+   adapters; hidden production presentation integration and resource cycles;
+   contained parent death/emergency; negative build/evidence/package tests.
+   Use bounded calls and preserve exact build/test identities. Research primary
+   Windows/Windhawk documentation for changed platform mechanisms.
+5. **Phase 6 beta:** emit version `1.0.0-beta.1`, a self-contained mod source,
+   reproducible source/tooling ZIP, checksums, machine-readable build/evidence
+   records, release notes, install/upgrade/remove guidance, read-only diagnostic
+   tooling and a qualification matrix. Validate the ZIP contents against the
+   compiled source and reproduce its hash.
+
+Beta means an internal testing artifact. No public release, commit/push,
+Windhawk installation or automatic desktop activation is included. Original
+source licensing/public naming remain separate publication decisions. Preserve
+the historical candidate and Phase 1 reports. Complete beta work without
+asking for physical testing; remaining desktop evidence stays in LOOP-016.
