+   simply remove the age check while attributing historical input to the current
+   cursor position. Historical keyboard focus requires separate treatment.
+2. Remove routine blocking filesystem and shell maintenance from the input-critical
+   thread. Cache/background-refresh power fault state with explicit invalidation
+   on topology, power operations and fault reset. Update the tray on state changes
+   and retain controlled recovery when Explorer/tray becomes unavailable.
+3. Keep immediate wake/reconciliation lightweight. Preserve independent monitors,
+   explicit shared/pointer/foreground scopes, keyboard semantics, spanning sessions,
+   sticky sessions, event-before-manual-start rejection, session/topology generations,
+   disabled displays and power permission/quarantine boundaries.
