+# Windhawk V1 production implementation handoff
+
+Continue in the existing checkout `E:\Citadel\oled_aegis`, implementing the Windhawk V1 plan under [D-0007](../../state/DECISIONS.md). The operator has decided to proceed without hands-on testing. Complete as much production implementation, automated verification, and documentation as possible through Phases 2–6. Do not ask the operator to perform desktop tests or stop merely because physical multi-monitor evidence is unavailable.
+
+This is the single active production handoff. The earlier [feasibility handoff](windhawk-v1-implementation-handoff.md) and [Phase 1 report](../../../windhawk/docs/PHASE_1_REPORT.md) are historical inputs. Do not rerun Phase 0 from scratch, reopen closed audit curation, or enforce the superseded requirement to pass the physical-desktop gate before writing production code.
+
+## Establish context
+
+Follow [AGENTS.md](../../../AGENTS.md) and its startup reads. Read the [accepted V1 plan](../plans/WINDHAWK_V1.md), latest decisions, [OPEN_LOOPS.md](../../state/OPEN_LOOPS.md), local development rules, Phase 1 report, and the existing acceptance, compatibility, provenance, and audit-disposition documents under `windhawk/docs/`. Inspect the current branch/diff and compiler installation. Preserve intentional uncommitted planning and prototype work. Use the existing checkout; do not create another repository or worktree that omits those files. Only one agent may write this repository at a time.
+
+Keep the entire P01-P11/S01-S08 feature contract: minimal inherited code migration, stock Windows savers, tray icon, existing intended behavior, attribution, and independent monitor operation. Missing manual tests change the available evidence, not the requested features. Do not silently replace screensavers with black output or remove media/input modes to make tests easier.
+
+## What the feasibility work established
+
+The installed Windhawk compiler built the original prototype and same-source harness. Installed stock savers created hosted child windows in isolated probes. Owned child-tree containment, failure paths, and emergency cleanup have partial runtime evidence. Exact observations and artifact identities are in the report; preserve their qualifications.
+
+The test graphics session exposed one output; tray creation failed there. Actual Windhawk loading, callbacks, unload, visible animation, physical input, and simultaneous displays remain unverified. The prototype's emergency worker can wait behind a session lock held during launch, shutdown uses final indefinite joins, launch health is not monitored, and monitor indexes are not persistent identities. Review and replace these assumptions for production rather than simply renaming the prototype.
+
+## Implementation scope
+
+Create the production mod under `windhawk/mods/`, with focused helpers/tests under `windhawk/` as useful. Keep `windhawk/prototype/` and its evidence as the experiment baseline. Keep inherited standalone source, assets, build entry points, product documentation, and legacy CI unchanged. Generated outputs and raw local test data belong in ignored `build/windhawk/`. A separate Windhawk-only build/test workflow is allowed if useful, with no publication side effects.
+
+Continue using original implementation wherever practical. Reuse reviewed code from our prototype selectively; record external copied/adapted material and dependencies in PROVENANCE. Do not copy inherited source/assets whose rights remain unresolved. Maintain inspiration credits even when no code is reused. Public naming, original-code licensing, and dependency notices must be accurately recorded; unknown rights are not resolved by assigning a license label.
+
+Do not modify managed Writ, remotes, Windows startup/lock/power policies, unrelated mods, or another repository. No commit, push, public release, or Windhawk collection submission is included. Source implementation and local build/test/package preparation are included.
+
+## Work sequence
+
+### 1 Production lifecycle and state
+
+Define explicit ownership for UI windows, tray, timers, workers, COM objects, settings snapshots, monitor sessions, child processes, and jobs. Implement reliable init, settings changes, partial-init failure, pause/exit, and unload. Ensure no worker can execute unloaded DLL code. Avoid locks shared with the emergency path across potentially blocking launch/query operations. Document any OS-level wait whose bound cannot be guaranteed; never use forced thread termination as a cleanup shortcut.
+
+Use a testable controller driven by monotonic time and explicit observations. Give each monitor a stable identity and retain disconnected-monitor settings. Use session generations to reject stale asynchronous results. Derive tray state from actual monitor states. Configuration must have one validated, versioned source of truth and report persistence failures.
+
+First milestone: production source compiles under the selected stable Windhawk toolchain, focused controller/configuration tests pass, and existing containment tests exercise the production lifecycle where possible. This is not a full V1 completion claim.
+
+### 2 Restore intended feature parity
+
+Implement P01-P11: global/per-monitor idle modes, all documented settings/ranges, media and muted-media controls, black overlays and edge padding, tray actions/settings, recovery, startup adaptation, and explicit legacy configuration import. Correct the inherited failure scenarios recorded in the audit. Preserve the original configuration file on import and avoid retaining duplicate automatic startup without a clearly documented migration action.
+
+Preserve conservative, documented input/media attribution. No claim of perfect browser-tab attribution. Test all input/media mode combinations and worst-case configured polling intervals. Failed or stale media observations must have a defined policy. Automatic activation is a implemented user preference, but do not enable unattended operation on the operator's desktop merely to test it.
+
+### 3 Integrate stock screensavers
+
+Implement per-monitor stock-saver discovery/assignment, preview/configure actions, independent sessions, bounded launch-health observation, no-relaunch-loop fallback, owned-process containment, graceful stop followed by cleanup, and handling of session/power/topology changes. Allow different savers or black on different displays. Keep display sleep effective and exclude owned saver activity from self-sustaining media suppression.
+
+Use fully qualified installed paths and argument serialization; do not bundle or download Windows savers. No forced reparenting of arbitrary fullscreen windows. Make compatibility and failure diagnostics useful without exposing private photo contents, titles, or input data. A process that remains alive or creates a child window is not proof of correct rendering; do not market heuristic startup checks as such.
+
+### 4 Automated verification and review
+
+Separate pure policy tests, platform-adapter tests, harness integration checks, and real Windhawk evidence in test output. Use injected clocks, topology/input/media observations, process outcomes, and storage failures to cover the behavior that unavailable hardware cannot exercise. Run meaningful tests through production logic rather than maintaining a separate toy implementation solely for tests.
+
+Cover all-disabled persistence, reorder/reconnect and negative coordinates, mixed-DPI geometry calculations, timer boundaries, clock changes, input between polls, stale callbacks, media ambiguity, failed process queries, settings changes during sessions, missing/early-exit/hung children, duplicate sessions, parent death, partial initialization, and repeated cleanup. Test malformed/Unicode/long configuration paths and failed writes. Repeat the established real process-containment checks using the production path where practical.
+
+Use bounded tool/test calls and emit evidence before any potentially slow UI operation. The earlier combined desktop call stalled; do not repeat it indefinitely. Automated non-disruptive desktop checks are useful if available, but do not fabricate multiple physical displays with simulated events or treat a shell-less tray failure as proof of real desktop behavior. Do not request hands-on testing. Leave those entries deferred with the environment limitation and proceed.
+
+Run suitable automated resource/lifecycle endurance checks in the available environment. Distinguish controller/harness soak from actual saver/GPU/display soak. Do not repeat successful tests without a code change or unresolved concern. Review executable launch, owned-resource cleanup, persistence, logging, and supply-chain inputs before packaging.
+
+### 5 Documentation and candidate package
+
+Update `windhawk/README.md` for the production candidate, keeping the prototype instructions separately reachable. Document installation/removal, settings, startup dependence, migration, saver assignment, fallback, limitations, credits, third-party notices, and verified prerequisites. Preserve exact build commands and reproducible source packaging for Windhawk; validate the distributed source format rather than relying only on a raw locally linked DLL.
+
+Maintain `ACCEPTANCE.md`, `COMPATIBILITY.md`, and `PROVENANCE.md` as the evidence registers. Add `windhawk/docs/PRODUCTION_REPORT.md` for implementation coverage, tests, package identity, residual defects, and deferred qualification. No stock saver should gain a supported label merely because source code exists or a harness probe passed.
+
+## Completion and stopping rules
+
+Continue through the work sequence without routine milestone approval requests. Resolve ordinary implementation choices using the plan and report material deviations. Physical-desktop test availability is not a blocker under D-0007. Hardware-dependent evidence remains deferred under LOOP-016; do not mark it passed or erase the historical Phase 1 result.
+
+An acceptable completed implementation assignment is a V1 candidate with all required behavior implemented, appropriate available automated checks passing, remaining defects addressed or explicitly reported, attribution/package materials prepared, and unavailable qualification clearly listed. Describe it as **implementation complete with desktop qualification outstanding** when that is the evidence. Do not call it fully runtime-validated, universally compatible, or a supported stable release.
+
+Stop early only for a genuine blocker after completing independent work, or an execution limit requiring a checkpoint. Preserve exact resumption commands and the next concrete action. Do not substitute a repeated request for manual testing for implementation progress. Ask only for information/authority genuinely required beyond the accepted scope; publication remains a separate action.
+
+Update LOOP-015, LOOP-016, and work-log evidence without mixing retained standalone defects with the new edition. Return the production source/report paths, implemented coverage, meaningful test results, known defects, deferred qualification, and any remaining work. Leave everything reviewable and uncommitted.
