+  Also [MathWorks MSAC algorithm](https://www.mathworks.com/help/vision/ref/estimategeometrictransform2d.html)
+  and [Maryland State Arts Council](https://msac.org/about).
+- SMAC: [Windows MAC-address utility](https://smac-tool.com/) and
+  [AutoML SMAC3 / smac package](https://github.com/automl/SMAC3).
+- DAC: [TI digital-to-analog converters](https://www.ti.com/product-category/data-converters/dacs/overview.html).
+- MIC: [Windows Mandatory Integrity Control](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/secauthz/mandatory-integrity-control).
+- DSC: [VESA Display Stream Compression](https://vesa.org/vesa-display-compression-codecs/dsc/)
+  and [Microsoft Desired State Configuration](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/scripting/dsc/overview).
+
+Recommendation is comparative: MSAC remains the least confusing fit for this
+monitor utility among these candidates, but is not unique; pair it with its
+full descriptive title and consider `msac-display` for a more specific identity.
+SMAC overlaps a Windows utility and DSC directly overlaps monitor terminology;
+DAC/MIC are overloaded technical abbreviations. No name chosen, no source,
+release, ID or configuration-folder changes.
